# 113: SHADOW (the "?" 5-START-press code) vs a TENANT — the morph test.
# Built 14z-116 to answer the maintainer's question: does the game break
# when Shadow faces one of the three ported characters, INCLUDING the quiet
# failure "Shadow takes the SHELL character instead of the tenant"?
#
# THE CODE, decoded 14z-116 (docs/game/atlas/select_screen.md): on the "?"
# cell 0x0B, FIVE START PRESSES arm $43 (PRG:0x020CB0 `cmpi.b #$5,$42(a6)`,
# gated on btst #15 of the EDGE word d3 — presses, not a hold); confirming
# then sets $3BC (PRG:0x020AB4). At each ROUND/MATCH END the winner-flagged
# player takes the LOSER's id and palette, UNMASKED (PRG:0x009BB2).
#
# PATHS ARE COMPUTED FROM THE MERGED BUILD'S OWN TABLE B, NOT VANILLA'S:
#   P1 default 0x01 -> D 0x06 -> D 0x08 -> DR 0x0B   ("?")
#   P2 default 0x05 -> L 0x0A -> D 0x09 -> D 0x13    (Donovan)
# Our port re-pointed 0x08's DOWN edge to 0x10 (Phobos), so vanilla's
# D,D,D route to "?" does NOT exist on a WIDE build — that mistake sent the
# first run to Phobos and cost a rebuild.
#
# P1 then walks in and mashes to a round win over an idle P2 Donovan.
# MEASURED on build/m3b_merged18: at the round end P1's id flips 0x00 ->
# 0x13 and the loader installs DONOVAN'S OWN record 0x003FA9D0 (not
# Victor's 0x0009769E shell); the HUD reads "Donovan" and the art is his.
# Guard-clean END 21120 through several further morphs.
# ONLY THE FIRST MORPH IS DETERMINISTIC — after P2 is beaten the flow falls
# into the arcade draw, which is the sound-fed lottery ([VSE-79]). Assert
# nothing about frames past ~8500.
300-305 sys=C1
330-335 sys=C2
800-803 sys=S1
830-833 sys=S2
1000-1002 p1=D
1040-1042 p1=D
1080-1082 p1=DR
1010-1012 p2=L
1050-1052 p2=D
1090-1092 p2=D
1200-1202 sys=S1
1240-1242 sys=S1
1280-1282 sys=S1
1320-1322 sys=S1
1360-1362 sys=S1
# RE-TIMED 14z-117b (random select includes the tenants): the "?" draw now
# cycles the tenants too, so the old confirm (1450) landed on THIS BUILD'S
# tenant on every solo (a mirror match; the morph verdict went vacuous).
# The solo cycle (period 48) and the merged cycle (54) coincide at 1499+3k:
# frames 1520-1522 show Bulleta (0x00) on all four builds — the character
# the fight script below was written for. Confirm registers one frame
# early (input staged ahead), so 1521-1522 lands inside that plateau.
# Measured 14z-117b: P1 0x00 at 3000, morph to 0x13/Donovan's record at 7800
# on don_m17 AND merged20 with the fight lines unshifted.
1521-1522 p1=1
1500-1502 p2=1
# P1 walks in and mashes to a MATCH WIN over an idle P2 Donovan, so the
# WIN SCREEN runs with $3BC set on the winner and a TENANT as the loser —
# the PRG:0x009BB2 path (a0=$13a winner, a1=$13c loser).
